{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794184716,"nonce":"7ilMVaTh9BbPts7BHwLZYgF3YnY=","title":"Host interop: Rust twins of shader structs, typed overrides, bind group layout constants","message":"Every shader struct gets a generated Rust twin with the WGSL layout (offsets and padding from naga's layouter), bytemuck Pod and a const size assert. Each #[override] const becomes a field of a generated Overrides struct that yields wgpu's (name, f64) list. Groups, bindings, vertex input locations, target locations, member offsets and block sizes become associated consts, as HXSL emits them.\n\nOpen: how a struct shared by shaders in several crates is declared once (a types library re-exported by both, or the build driver).\n\nDepends on the core language issue (8fad30d).","files":null}]}